From: TripleU <182648541+TripleU613@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 11:35:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] soc: apple: sleep: admit a binned part with fewer cores
 than the profile's machine

The J714s profile was measured on the 18-core M5 Pro. The 15-core M5 Pro
J714s has the same boot MPIDR and three clusters of five cores, and the
CPU inventory check refused it ("unsupported CPU inventory"), so it only
offered s2idle. Accept fewer possible CPUs than the profile's count; the
loop below still checks each core's cluster, core number, MPIDR and
CPU-start bit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c
@@ -2219,8 +2219,12 @@
 		return dev_err_probe(s->dev, -EINVAL, "invalid CPU-start geometry\n");
 
 	/* The node's compatible chose the profile: its machine is where it was measured */
+	/*
+	 * A binned part of the same machine has fewer cores (the 15-core M5 Pro J714s against the
+	 * 18-core one the profile was measured on); every core it does have is checked below.
+	 */
 	if (soc->machine && (cpu_logical_map(0) != soc->boot_mpidr ||
-			     num_possible_cpus() != soc->cpu_count))
+			     num_possible_cpus() > soc->cpu_count))
 		return dev_err_probe(s->dev, -EINVAL, "unsupported CPU inventory\n");
 
 	index = of_property_match_string(np, "reg-names", "cpu-start");
-- 
